{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Why should he speak…, etc. like these things, etc.</b> Meaning: what place is there for such things? Not only the things themselves, but even that which resembles them is not fitting for him to speak — anything that resembles such a provocation, heaven forbid for your servants to do even something resembling this. And this is its saying <b>like these things.</b> And its saying <b>Behold, the silver, etc.</b> — he had already refuted this a fortiori argument, as I explained. They intended to overturn his claim both according to what we explained, for his intent was to say that they refuted the presumption of returning it, since it is not on account of their faithfulness but rather a chance occurrence. They said: it is true that such a thing could happen by chance for a robber to do like these things, but not in this order — that after he acquired it and transported it to a distant place for many days; even for a trustworthy man it is difficult for him to return stolen goods that have been consumed, and we returned it to you from the land of Canaan after we had acquired it at a distance — such a reality is found only in the category of one absolutely trustworthy. And against what he cleverly devised to say, that they intended deception in returning the silver — it is true that his words would be justified if the goblet were considered among them as an instrument of divination; then the matters would be as he claims. But according to the truth, it is among them like any other silver in general, for they do not divine nor do they know how to divine with it, and it is nothing to them except like any other silver. And this is its saying <b>How could we steal, etc.</b> <b>silver, etc.</b> — meaning: the goblet is nothing among us except in the category of silver. And what they said <b>or gold</b> — they intended to say that they do not know the goblet about which he is making a claim against them, whether it is silver or gold, and this would demonstrate that they have no knowledge of it whatsoever."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:31.130704807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}